---
title: Khao man gai
servings: 4
yield: 4 to 6 servings
tags: [chicken]
cuisine: thai
time: 2 hours
source: Khao Man Gai (Thai-Style Chicken and Rice) by Bryan Roof, America's Test Kitchen, https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/12928-thai-style-chicken-and-rice-khao-man-gai
---

== Chicken and broth ==

Put the @water{12%cups}, @ginger{2%inch piece}(peeled, sliced into 1/4-inch rounds),
@table salt{2%tbsp} and @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed) in a #Dutch oven{}
of at least 7 quarts.

Add the @whole chicken{1}(3 1/2 to 4 lb, giblets discarded) breast up and bring
to a simmer over high heat. Cover with foil and then the lid, turn the heat to
low, and simmer ~{25-35%minutes}, until the breast reads 160°F and the thighs
at least 175°F.

Lift the chicken into a bowl, tent it with foil and let it rest. Skim the
broth, measure out 3 cups for the rice, and cover the rest.

== Rice ==

In a #large saucepan{} over medium heat, cook the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp},
@shallot{1}(finely chopped), @ginger{2%inch piece}(peeled, halved lengthwise),
@garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @table salt{1/4%tsp} ~{2%minutes}, until the
shallot softens.

Add the @jasmine rice{2%cups}(rinsed) and stir ~{2%minutes}, until the edges of
the grains turn translucent.

Pour in the 3 cups of broth and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Cover,
turn the heat to low and cook ~{20%minutes}. Take it off the heat and leave it
covered ~{10%minutes} more without lifting the lid.

== Sauce ==

Whisk the @Thai soybean paste{1/4%cup}, @soy sauce{1/4%cup},
@white vinegar{1/4%cup}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @garlic{3%cloves}(minced),
@Thai chiles{2}(stemmed, minced) and @ginger{1%tsp}(grated) until the sugar
dissolves, about a minute.

== To serve ==

Bring the remaining broth back to a simmer over medium heat.

Pull the breasts off the bone and discard the skin. Cut off the leg quarters,
shred their meat with two forks, and discard the skin and bones. Slice the
breasts 1/2 inch thick.

Spread the rice on a platter, top with the shredded meat and then the sliced
breast. Pile the @cilantro{1%cup}(leaves and stems) in one corner and lay the
@cucumber{1/2}(English, thinly sliced) along the side.

Ladle the broth into bowls, about a cup each, and scatter the
@scallions{2}(thinly sliced) over. Serve with the chicken, rice and sauce.

> The sauce keeps two days in the fridge. The chicken and broth can be cooked a
> day ahead: refrigerate them together, then rewarm the pieces in the broth
> before slicing.
